--- ARTIFACT NOTES ---
Surface files (src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/ScoreBadge):
  ScoreBadge.kt      (view: score/grade stateful entries + stateless renderer + tone/size mappers + previews),
  ScoreBadgeModel.kt (pure port of scoreScale.ts numericToGrade/gradeInfo + GRADE_PALETTE tones + projection
                      + PII-safe view.opened diagnostics; SLUG=ScoreBadge).
  Web source is a pure presentational primitive (only hook = useTranslation) -> no P1/S8 Source/ViewModel
  (sibling BatteryDelta/Distance/Speed precedent). The web spec has no fetch, so no loading/error/stale/offline
  lifecycle is invented (honesty covenant: no scope narrowing, no silent drift). Reproduced states: the seven
  grade branches A+/A/B/C/D/F and the "—" no-score sentinel, across sizes sm/md/lg.

Color tokens (web GRADE_PALETTE hex -> P1/S9 token, exact in brand/dark theme):
  A+/A #10b981 -> status.success; B #00f0ff -> status.info; C #f59e0b -> status.warning;
  D #ef4444 / F #b91c1c -> status.danger (one semantic danger red; in high-contrast it is exactly the web F
  #b91c1c — the letter carries the D-vs-F distinction, per the web "the letter IS the badge" intent);
  — #6b7280 -> onSurfaceVariant (muted).
Size tokens (web SIZE_CLASS -> generated ramp): sm text-xs -> bodySmall (~12sp); md text-xl -> headlineSmall
  (~18sp, nearest ramp step to web 20); lg text-3xl -> displaySmall (~30sp). Bold + tabular figures applied.

Unit tests (run by the gate, testReleaseUnitTest): ScoreBadgeModelTest=11, ScoreBadgeDiagnosticsTest=3 -> 14
  tests, 0 failures. Cover the threshold mapping (default + caller scales + highest-first), the null/non-finite
  "—" guard, the gradeInfo tone+numeric palette, the score-/grade-driven projection, and the PII-safe diagnostic.

UI test (src/androidTest/.../scorebadge/ScoreBadgeUiTest.kt): per-state localized a11y label (Score A+/B/—),
  numeric-score->grade mapping, ariaLabel override, single-merged-a11y-node, size-invariance, and the one-shot
  view.opened. It executes under :android:connectedAndroidTest on a device/emulator (none on this runner), per
  the same split the sibling BatteryDelta/RouteAnnouncer UiTests document. NOTE: the androidTest source set as a
  whole does not compile on this runner — 20 PRE-EXISTING sibling files (dashboard/widgets/*, modals-dialogs/*,
  feature-views/*, sharedsurfaces/{routeannouncer,annotationlist,elevationprofile}) reference unresolved
  androidx.compose.ui.test symbols (assertExists/assertDoesNotExist/onAllNodes/assert). ScoreBadgeUiTest itself
  introduces no compile error (verified absent from the :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin diagnostic
  inventory) and passes ktlintAndroidTestSourceSetCheck. This is independent of ScoreBadge and outside the four
  gate steps (which run JVM unit tests, not instrumented compilation).

i18n: web ScoreBadge resolves score.aria ("Score {{grade}}") as an inline-default key absent from the catalog.
  Added to the canonical web/src/i18n/en.json and materialized as translation_score_aria ("Score %1$s") in
  values{,-ar,-he}/strings.xml (ar/he English fallback, per P1/S10 policy — mirrors the BatteryDelta predecessor).

Capability: Java 17 toolchain, Kotlin 2.x (>= 2.2.x floor), Compose BOM + Material3, Android SDK + AGP present;
  release build, JVM unit tests, ktlint + detekt all green. NOT blocked.

